# Godot conventions

- This is Godot 4 GDScript. Do not introduce C# / .NET unless the user explicitly switches the project.
- Never edit or commit `.godot/` — it is import cache. Regenerate with `godot --headless --path . --import`.
- Keep `res://` paths valid. After adding or renaming scenes/scripts, run headless import so `.uid` files stay consistent.
- Prefer text-format `.tscn` / `.tres`. Do not convert resources to binary unless asked.
- Put scenes in `scenes/`, gameplay scripts in `scripts/`, one-off CI/tool scripts in `tools/`.
- Do not change `uid://` identifiers on existing resources unless Godot regenerated them after a real rename.
- Playtest in the Godot editor on the machine that has this checkout. Cloud Agents are not the daily loop.
- MCP `godot` is the Coding-Solo CLI (run/log). MCP `godot-editor` is KeeVeeG and needs the Godot **editor** open with the Godot MCP plugin active, pointed at this Windows folder.
- Pin the editor with `.godot-version`. If you bump Godot, update that file and `config/features` in `project.godot` together.
